{"name":"Barnyard Grass","hex":"#5dac51","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"barnyard grass","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of barnyardgrass."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/barnyard_grass"}],"entries":[{"title":"Barnyard grass","blocks":[{"text":"Barnyard grass is a common name for several plants and may refer to:"},{"items":["Dactylis glomerata","Echinochloa crus-galli"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barnyard_grass"},{"title":"Echinochloa","blocks":[{"text":"Echinochloa is a very widespread genus of plants in the grass family and tribe Paniceae. Some of the species are known by the common names barnyard grass or cockspur grass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Echinochloa_crus-galli_2006.08.27_14.59.37-p8270051.jpg/330px-Echinochloa_crus-galli_2006.08.27_14.59.37-p8270051.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Echinochloa"},{"title":"Barnyard","blocks":[{"text":"A barnyard or farmyard is an enclosed or open yard adjoining a barn, and, typically, related farm buildings, including a farmhouse. Enclosed barnyards are usually formed by a combination of fences and farm structures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Traditional_Nottinghamshire_farmyard%2C_Lincoln_Rd%2C_Tuxford_-_geograph.org.uk_-_167753.jpg/330px-Traditional_Nottinghamshire_farmyard%2C_Lincoln_Rd%2C_Tuxford_-_geograph.org.uk_-_167753.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barnyard"},{"title":"Grass","blocks":[{"text":"Grass refers to various families of plants. The three major families of grasslike plants are true grasses (Poaceae), sedges (Cyperaceae), and rushes (Juncaceae). Lawns and pasturelands are typically composed of true grasses, five of which cover 46% of the world's arable land: rice, wheat, maize, barley, and sugar cane."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Poa_annua.jpg/330px-Poa_annua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Echinochloa_colona_%28Jungle_Rice%29_W2_IMG_0528.jpg/500px-Echinochloa_colona_%28Jungle_Rice%29_W2_IMG_0528.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Echinochloa_colona_%28Jungle_Rice%29_W2_IMG_0528.jpg/500px-Echinochloa_colona_%28Jungle_Rice%29_W2_IMG_0528.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"jungle rice (Echinochloa colona)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEchinochloa_colona_(Jungle_Rice)_W2_IMG_0528.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Farmyard_in_Winter_by_George_Henry_Durrie%2C_1858.jpg/500px-Farmyard_in_Winter_by_George_Henry_Durrie%2C_1858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Farmyard_in_Winter_by_George_Henry_Durrie%2C_1858.jpg/1280px-Farmyard_in_Winter_by_George_Henry_Durrie%2C_1858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Farmyard_in_Winter_by_George_Henry_Durrie%2C_1858.jpg/500px-Farmyard_in_Winter_by_George_Henry_Durrie%2C_1858.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A romantic painting titled Farmyard in Winter by George Henry Durrie, 1858, U.S.A.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFarmyard_in_Winter_by_George_Henry_Durrie%2C_1858.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}